# Terminal Recording: Check What the Keyless Setup Script Created (AWS)
# Target page: public/docs/connections/keyless-cloud-connections.md
# Placement: After "### Check What the Script Created" heading
# Duration target: 30 seconds
# Prerequisites: An AWS test account with a keyless Planton connection created in the console,
#   its setup script saved as keyless-aws.sh (copied from the console's Set Up step),
#   and the AWS CLI signed in to that account. Use a test organization and account whose
#   IDs are safe to show; do not record a customer's account.

## Setup (do these BEFORE starting the recording):
# 1. Clear terminal: clear
# 2. Resize terminal to 80x24
# 3. Set prompt to simple "$ " if possible
# 4. Replace <org> and <connection> below with the organization's and the connection's slugs

## Recording command:
# asciinema rec keyless-cloud-connections.cast --cols 80 --rows 24

## Commands to type (pause ~1s between each):

bash keyless-aws.sh
aws iam list-open-id-connect-providers
aws iam get-role --role-name planton-<org>-<connection> --query Role.AssumeRolePolicyDocument
curl -s https://planton.ai/.well-known/openid-configuration

## End recording:
# Type: exit
# Or press Ctrl+D

## Post-recording:
# Then click Check the Trust in the console wizard (not part of the recording).
# Convert to SVG: svg-term --in keyless-cloud-connections.cast --out keyless-cloud-connections.svg --window
# Upload: run `make sync-assets` in planton/site
